    ('0d70773f-7235-4afe-bfef-75ec938701b3'::uuid, 'card_description', 'An amateur, J. Medhurst, carried out the original digs at this Romano-Celtic temple. From 1843-6 he worked on a hill above a cove, where the Roman ruin of the temple still stands.', 'Above Bowleaze Cove, Jordan Hill Roman Temple is a Romano-Celtic ruin with a cemetery of cremations and inhumations and a precinct that held deposits of animal bones, ceramics and coins.', 'teaser-card-s044-rollback:0d70773f-7235-4afe-bfef-75ec938701b3:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s044: card_description ''Above Bowleaze Cove, Jordan Hill Roman Temple is a Romano-Celtic ruin with a cemetery of cremations and inhumations and a precinct that held deposits of animal bones, ceramics and coins.'' restored on Jordan Hill Roman Temple', 'ebb63e25d2346841568172832fae123cf7f74fc422812d3ff7ea683c56336ca8|9eba760e5a5e77f459ee8070926888c6c27a19271941103f8870b36ca6ca122b|9eba760e5a5e77f459ee8070926888c6c27a19271941103f8870b36ca6ca122b', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite1-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "An amateur, J. Medhurst, carried out the original digs at this Romano-Celtic temple. From 1843-6 he worked on a hill above a cove, where the Roman ruin of the temple still stands."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check1-001 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the original excavations at the site were amateur work [S2]; they were carried out by J. Medhurst [S2]; the site is a Romano-Celtic temple [S1]; the excavations took place in 1843-6 [S2]; the site lies on a hill above a cove [S1]; the temple is a Roman ruin that is there today (present tense ''is ... situated'') [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-001 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "J. Medhurst carried out the original digs at this Romano-Celtic temple [SUPPORTED: https://dorset-ancestors.com/?p=1693]; J. Medhurst was an amateur [SUPPORTED: https://web.prm.ox.ac.uk/england/englishness-James-Medhurst-and-Jordan-Hill.html]; The site is a Romano-Celtic temple [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/jordan-hill-roman-temple/history/]; Medhurst''s work began in 1843 [SUPPORTED: https://dorset-ancestors.com/?p=1693]; Medhurst''s work ran until 1846 [SUPPORTED: https://web.prm.ox.ac.uk/england/englishness-James-Medhurst-and-Jordan-Hill.html]; He worked on a hill [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/jordan-hill-roman-temple/history/]; The hill lies above a cove [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowleaze_Cove]; The Roman ruin of the temple still stands there [SUPPORTED: https://web.prm.ox.ac.uk/england/englishness-James-Medhurst-and-Jordan-Hill.html]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0d9dc1e0-d65e-4507-be51-4c2220ba8de3'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Four rectangular towers marked the corners of an 80 x 90 m compound. Inside stood a basilica with three aisles and the bishop of Pydna''s home, on the road between Thessaloniki and Larissa.', 'A fortified early Christian bishop''s seat from the Byzantine era, found during railway construction. Its mosaics and basilica reveal the wealth of provincial Christianity in Late Antiquity.', 'teaser-card-s044-rollback:0d9dc1e0-d65e-4507-be51-4c2220ba8de3:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s044: card_description "A fortified early Christian bishop''s seat from the Byzantine era, found during railway construction. Its mosaics and basilica reveal the wealth of provincial Christianity in Late Antiquity." restored on Louloudies', '47e077068b5425e98d39f9eccbd7751100570f7459b781b1df49aba3bef66d6c|ce4fb7f01013584146512166526282fb44b91919d7ea7486f1609c7ba84d1c86|ce4fb7f01013584146512166526282fb44b91919d7ea7486f1609c7ba84d1c86', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite-v-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Four rectangular towers marked the corners of an 80 x 90 m compound. Inside stood a basilica with three aisles and the bishop of Pydna''s home, on the road between Thessaloniki and Larissa."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-v-001 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "four rectangular towers stood at the corners of the walls [S2]; the compound measured 80 x 90 m [S2]; the compound was walled [S2]; inside stood a basilica [S2]; the basilica had three aisles [S2]; inside stood the bishop''s residence [S2]; the bishop was the bishop of Pydna, who resided here [S3]; the complex lies on the road between Thessaloniki and Larissa [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify2-001 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Towers marked the corners of the compound [SUPPORTED: https://el.wikipedia.org/wiki/%CE%9B%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%BB%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%B4%CE%B9%CE%AD%CF%82_%CE%A0%CE%B9%CE%B5%CF%81%CE%AF%CE%B1%CF%82]; There were four towers [SUPPORTED: https://golden-greece.gr/en/archaeological/makedonia/pieria/episkopiko-sygkrotima-louloudies-kitrous]; The towers were rectangular [SUPPORTED: https://el.wikipedia.org/wiki/%CE%9B%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%BB%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%B4%CE%B9%CE%AD%CF%82_%CE%A0%CE%B9%CE%B5%CF%81%CE%AF%CE%B1%CF%82]; The compound measured 80 x 90 m [SUPPORTED: https://golden-greece.gr/en/archaeological/makedonia/pieria/episkopiko-sygkrotima-louloudies-kitrous]; Inside the compound stood a basilica [SUPPORTED: https://golden-greece.gr/en/archaeological/makedonia/pieria/episkopiko-sygkrotima-louloudies-kitrous]; The basilica had three aisles [SUPPORTED: https://golden-greece.gr/en/archaeological/makedonia/pieria/episkopiko-sygkrotima-louloudies-kitrous]; Inside the compound stood the bishop''s home [SUPPORTED: https://golden-greece.gr/en/archaeological/makedonia/pieria/episkopiko-sygkrotima-louloudies-kitrous]; The bishop whose home stood there was the bishop of Pydna [SUPPORTED: https://www.mytraveler.gr/place/%CE%B5%CF%80%CE%B9%CF%83%CE%BA%CE%BF%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C-%CF%83%CF%85%CE%B3%CE%BA%CF%81%CF%8C%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%BC%CE%B1-%CF%83%CF%84%CE%B9%CF%82-%CE%BB%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%BB%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%B4%CE%B9%CE%AD%CF%82-%CE%BA%CE%AF%CF%84%CF%81%CE%BF%CF%85%CF%82]; The compound stood on the road between Thessaloniki and Larissa [SUPPORTED: https://www.mytraveler.gr/place/%CE%B5%CF%80%CE%B9%CF%83%CE%BA%CE%BF%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C-%CF%83%CF%85%CE%B3%CE%BA%CF%81%CF%8C%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%BC%CE%B1-%CF%83%CF%84%CE%B9%CF%82-%CE%BB%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%BB%CE%BF%CF%85%CE%B4%CE%B9%CE%AD%CF%82-%CE%BA%CE%AF%CF%84%CF%81%CE%BF%CF%85%