    ('1010b3bf-a7d5-4e2c-9f70-8212a2cd1699'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Looted Maya reliefs from a city then unknown surfaced on the art market in the 1960s. Later, this Maya court residence was found and identified as their long-sought source.', 'In the 1960s looted Maya reliefs from an unknown city surfaced on the art market. They came from La Corona in Petén, the long-sought Site Q, whose old name seems to have been White-Flower.', 'teaser-card-s044-rollback:1010b3bf-a7d5-4e2c-9f70-8212a2cd1699:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s044: card_description ''In the 1960s looted Maya reliefs from an unknown city surfaced on the art market. They came from La Corona in Petén, the long-sought Site Q, whose old name seems to have been White-Flower.'' restored on La Corona', 'c9785ff168363240578473558694639c59449cf4f8c05017f3dcf8583d138db2|b2bc8dbd7c13a89e29441405c2664e08db27253144be8898c9b33e0ad5b8e993|b2bc8dbd7c13a89e29441405c2664e08db27253144be8898c9b33e0ad5b8e993', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite-v-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Looted Maya reliefs from a city then unknown surfaced on the art market in the 1960s. Later, this Maya court residence was found and identified as their long-sought source."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-v-001 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "looted Maya reliefs surfaced on the (international) art market [S3]; the reliefs came from a city that was then unknown [S3]; this happened in the 1960s [S3]; the site is a Maya court residence [S1]; the site was found later than the reliefs surfaced [S1, S3]; the site was identified as the long-sought source of those reliefs [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify2-001 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "This Maya court residence was identified as the long-sought source of the looted reliefs [SUPPORTED: https://www.mesoweb.com/reports/SiteQ.html]; The reliefs were looted [SUPPORTED: https://www.mesoweb.com/LaCorona/LaCoronaNotes01.pdf]; The reliefs were Maya reliefs [SUPPORTED: https://www.mesoweb.com/LaCorona/LaCoronaNotes02.pdf]; The reliefs came from a city then unknown [SUPPORTED: https://www.mesoweb.com/LaCorona/LaCoronaNotes02.pdf]; The reliefs surfaced on the art market [SUPPORTED: https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/article/maya-empire-snake-kings-dynasty-mesoamerica]; The reliefs surfaced in the 1960s [SUPPORTED: https://www.mesoweb.com/LaCorona/LaCoronaNotes02.pdf]; The site is a Maya court residence [SUPPORTED: http://www.asociaciontikal.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/14-Canuto-et-al_compressed.pdf]; The site was found later, after the reliefs had surfaced [SUPPORTED: https://www.mesoweb.com/reports/SiteQ.html]; The source of the reliefs had long been sought [SUPPORTED: https://www.mesoweb.com/LaCorona/LaCoronaNotes01.pdf]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('15e0fbf2-7d64-46c8-a5ed-8b8830b17b9c'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Three aligned henges, almost identical, sit on a raised plateau above a river. Each one is about 240 metres across, with two large entrances set directly opposite each other.', 'On a plateau above the River Ure, the Thornborough Henges form three almost identical rings, each approximately 240 metres across, with a cursus running beneath the central one.', 'teaser-card-s044-rollback:15e0fbf2-7d64-46c8-a5ed-8b8830b17b9c:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s044: card_description ''On a plateau above the River Ure, the Thornborough Henges form three almost identical rings, each approximately 240 metres across, with a cursus running beneath the central one.'' restored on Thornborough Henges', '29843a3a63956c1940211781b730827b613257b8d1d6b12d6bd4bab72420db08|4d7b4607409c6f72c2725c3a6eaf6ffd9acdf74de5209db44e2b8ef5b61c4079|4d7b4607409c6f72c2725c3a6eaf6ffd9acdf74de5209db44e2b8ef5b61c4079', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: writer card_writer:teaser-write-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Three aligned henges, almost identical, sit on a raised plateau above a river. Each one is about 240 metres across, with two large entrances set directly opposite each other."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-001 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site has three henges [S1, S5]; the three henges are aligned [S1]; the henges are almost identical [S5]; they sit on a raised plateau above a river [S2]; each henge is about 240 metres across [S5]; each henge has two large entrances [S5]; the two entrances are set directly opposite each other [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-001 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Three aligned henges sit at this site [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/thornborough-henges/history/]; The three henges are almost identical [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/thornborough-henges/history/]; The henges still sit there today (present tense) [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/thornborough-henges/history/]; They sit on a raised plateau [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/thornborough-henges/history/]; The plateau lies above a river [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/thornborough-henges/history/]; Each henge is about 240 metres across [SUPPORTED: http://www.stone-circles.org.uk/stone/thornborough.htm]; Each henge has two large entrances [SUPPORTED: http://www.stone-circles.org.uk/stone/thornborough.htm]; The two entrances are set directly opposite each other [SUPPORTED: https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/thornborough-henges/history/]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('16419886-7d47-4007-86ae-2fef6dd1fa38'::uuid, 'card_description', 'An arched tunnel runs from north to south at ground level in this Buddhist stupa. Stairs on the north side lead to the top, and mud mortar binds the mud bricks and baked bricks.', 'Near Johi in Sindh rises Thul Hairo Khan, a Buddhist stupa 50 feet high of mud and baked bricks, built possibly between the 5th and 7th centuries CE, an arched tunnel at its foot.', 'teaser-card-s044-rollback:16419886-7d47-4007-86ae-2fef6dd1fa38:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s044: card_description ''Near Johi in Sindh rises Thul Hairo Khan, a Buddhist stupa 50 feet high of mud and baked bricks, built possibly between the 5th and 7th centuries CE, an arched tunnel at its foot.'' restored on Thul Hairo Khan', '1988fba47a6e74eeb1636fd9e446172be1992b4e37dd8fc0597f9aba5232ffc6|35ebdcfa618ccb2b7c189772a97cf0b20708d7d142d5e7dd8c0d91fc58a917bf|35ebdcfa618ccb2b7c189772a97cf0b20708d7d142d5e7dd8c0d91fc58a917bf', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: writer card_writer:teaser-write-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "An arched tunnel runs from north to south at ground level in this Buddhist stupa. Stairs on the north side lead to the top, and mud mortar binds the mud bricks and baked bricks."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-001 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is a Buddhist stupa [S1]; it has an arched tunnel [S4]; the tunnel runs from north to south [S4]; the tunnel lies at ground level [S4]; stairs on the north side lead to the top [S3]; mud mortar binds mud bricks and baked bricks [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-001 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "An arched tunnel runs from north to south at ground level in this stupa [SUPPORTED: http://heritage.eftsindh.com/districts/dadu/hairo-khan-thul.php]; The site is a stupa [SUPPORTED: http://heritage.eftsindh.com/districts/dadu/hairo-khan-thul.php]; The stupa is Buddhist [SUPPORTED: http://heritage.eftsindh.com/districts/dadu/hairo-khan-thul.php]; Stairs lead to the top [SUPPORTED: http://heritage.eftsindh.com/districts/dadu/hairo-khan-thul.php]; The stairs are on the north side [SUPPORTED: http://heritage.eftsindh.com/districts/dadu/hairo-khan-thul.php]; The stupa is built of mud bricks and baked bricks [SUPPORTED: http://heritage.eftsindh.com/districts/dadu/hairo-khan-thul.php]; Mud mortar binds the bricks [SUPPORTED: http://heritage.eftsindh.com/districts/dadu/hairo-khan-thul.php]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1724deb2-8bac-4a38-971b-4d1542745e0b'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Four large capstones roof a chamber around 5 metres long in this tomb. George Bonsor excavated the tomb in 1900, and it is one of the best examples of a Scillonian entrance grave.', 'On a steep slope of St Mary''s, a roofless entrance leads past a jamb into the burial chamber of Bant''s Carn, a Bronze Age entrance grave roofed by four large capstones.', 'teaser-card-s044-rollback:1724deb2-8bac-4a38-971b-4d1542745e0b:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s044: card_description "On a steep slope of St Mary''s, a roofless entrance leads past a jamb into the burial chamber of Bant''s Carn, a Bronze Age entrance grave roofed by four large capstones." restored on Bant''s Carn', '9e1e6505b1e14ce0613367fd42c0b6af8c74daa5f62db3b98a4cd5588cda34fc|c2dfcaa6682b89f2233a5de3cef858492b498c6f353247d0a77144d781bf2e92|c2dfcaa6682b89f2233a5de3cef858492b498c6f353247d0a77144d781bf2e92', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: writer card_writer:teaser-write-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Four large capstones roof a chamber around 5 metres long in this tomb. George Bonsor excavated the tomb in 1900, and it is one of the best examples of a Scillonian entrance grave."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-001 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is a tomb with a chamber [S1, S2]; four large capstones roof the chamber [S2]; the chamber is around 5 metres long [S2]; George Bonsor excavated the tomb [S3]; the excavation took place in 1900 [S3]; it is one of the best examples of a Scillonian entrance grave [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-001 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a1-2026-11-07/OU